<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Keren</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-african-campaign-world-war-ii">East African campaign (World War II)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keren">Keren</a> was fought from February to March 1941 in the mountains around the town of Keren in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a>, between Italian forces and British and Indian troops. After weeks of costly attacks on the strong Italian positions, the British broke through on 27 March. The victory led to the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asmara">Asmara</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massawa">Massawa</a> and the end of Italian rule in Eritrea.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-keren.jpg" alt="Battle of Keren" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James Francis (Frank) Hurley · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indian_troops_stand_next_to_a_Cheren_(Keren)_signpost,_May_1941.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
